  "title": "JWT Overview",
  "description": "Understand JSON Web Tokens and their structure.",
  "order": 1,
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedMinutes": 20,
  "tags": ["jwt", "token", "structure", "overview"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**JWT (JSON Web Token)** is a compact, URL-safe means of representing claims to be transferred between two parties. It's commonly used for authentication."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "JWT Structure"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "A JWT consists of three parts separated by dots: `header.payload.signature`"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "JWT Structure",
        "content": "Example JWT",
        "language": "text",
        "code": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.  // Header\neyJzdWIiOiIxMjM0NTY3ODkwIiwibmFtZSI6IkFsaWNlIiwiaWF0IjoxNTE2MjM5MDIyfQ.  // Payload\nSflKxwRJSMeKKF2QT4fwpMeJf36POk6yJV_adQssw5c  // Signature"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Parts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Header**: Token type and signing algorithm",
          "**Payload**: Claims (user data, expiration)",
          "**Signature**: Verifies token integrity"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "data": {
        "variant": "warning",
        "title": "Not Encrypted",
        "text": "JWT payload is base64-encoded, not encrypted. Don't put sensitive data in JWTs."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "summary-box",
      "data": {
        "title": "Key Takeaways",
        "points": [
          "JWT has three parts: header, payload, signature",
          "Compact and URL-safe",
          "Contains claims about the user",
          "Not encrypted - don't store secrets"
        ],
        "takeaway": "JWTs are the standard for token-based auth."
      }
    }
  ],
